# Bandit Level 1 → Level 2

## Goal
Reading the file name '-' in the home directory to find the location of the password for the next level

## Commands used
ls
cat ./-

## Explanation
ls to list all the file in the directory
cat ./- to read the file named '-'
./ refers to the current directory and makes its clear that - is a filename. Using cat - would make cat wait for an input from the terminal instead

## Result
I gained the password from the filename '-' to advance to the next stage to bandit2

## What I learned
How to read file with that has a dash and ./ helps identify a file in the current directory.
